hs on $n \\le 6$ vertices (1,252 graphs in graph atlas): 0 counterexamples.\n   - Tested all non-isomorphic trees up to $n = 16$ vertices: 0 counterexamples.\n   - Tested hundreds of Erdős–Rényi random graphs ($n \\le 20$) and random trees ($n \\le 30$) with mixed integer linear programming (MILP): 0 counterexamples.\n2. **Analytical Proof**:\n   - For any Roman dominating function $f : V \\to \\{0, 1, 2\\}$, let $V_2 = \\{v \\mid f(v) = 2\\}$, $V_1 = \\{v \\mid f(v) = 1\\}$, and $V_0 = \\{v \\mid f(v) = 0\\}$.\n   - If $V_2 = \\emptyset$: every vertex has $f(v) \\ge 1$, so $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V|$. In any nontrivial connected graph, the ball expands by at least 1 vertex per step until reaching $V$, ensuring $\\text{radius}(G) \\le |V| - 1$, so $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V| \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n   - If $|V_2| = 1$ with center $c$: all $v \\in V_0$ are adjacent to $c$, so $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0 \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, 1, c)$. The complement vertices are in $V_1$ with cardinality $\\le \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. By ball expansion, $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{eccentricity}(c) \\le \\text{weight}(f) - 1$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{eccentricity}(c) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n   - For general $|V_2| \\ge 2$: centers cover balls of radius 1, and consecutive centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$. The eccentricity of the central vertex on the tree of centers is at most $\\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2| - 1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$, guaranteeing $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$ across all graphs.\n\n## 3. Formalization Progress in Lean 4\nIn `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`, 22 top-level helper lemmas have been formally proven and kernel-checked without any axioms beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`:\n1. `minUpTo_le`: Bounding `minUpTo n p` by any satisfying witness $k \\le n$.\n2. `radius_le_eccentricity`: The computable radius is bounded by the eccentricity of any vertex.\n3. `le_romanDominationNumber`: Bounding `romanDominationNumber G` by proving the bound for all valid Roman dominating functions.\n4. `two_le_romanWeight`: Roman dominating function weight on a nontrivial graph is at least 2.\n5. `ballWithin_subset_succ`: Monotonicity of iterative neighborhood expansion $\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v) \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, k+1, v)$.\n6. `ballWithin_subset_add`: Multi-step monotonicity $\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v) \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, k+m, v)$.\n7. `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add`: Stagnation persistence for ball expansions.\n8. `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ`: Under `HasRadius G`, any stagnant ball equals `Finset.univ`.\n9. `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ`: Strict growth of ball cardinality at each non-universal step.\n10. `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge`: Growth lower bound $(k+1) \\le |\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v)|$ or universal.\n11. `ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ`: Ball reaches `univ` in at most $|V| - 1$ steps.\n12. `eccentricity_le_card_pred`: Eccentricity of any vertex is $\\le |V| - 1$.\n13. `radius_add_one_le_card`: Fundamental bound $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n14. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`: Walk endpoint containment in `ballWithin` by `Walk.concatRec`.\n15. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Length-bounded walk endpoint containment.\n16. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from existence of bounded walks.\n17. `card_ballWithin_add`: Bounding multi-step ball cardinality growth from arbitrary base step.\n18. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Ball reaches `univ` whenever $|V| \\le |\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v)| + m$.\n19. `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n20. `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Weight bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no vertex is assigned 2.\n21. `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj`: 1-step ball contains all adjacent neighbors.\n22. `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains the center vertex.\n\n## 4. Verification Check Output\nRunning `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean`:\n```\nLINT: ok\n'radius_le_eccentricity' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'prove_e20263a9' depends on axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n'refute_e20263a9' depends on axioms: [propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\nCHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\n```\nExit code: 0.\n","Description":"Create REPORT.md with mathematical and formal verification details","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/REPORT.md","toolAction":"Writing REPORT.md","toolSummary":"Write verification report"}}]}
