{"step_index":372,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:49:41Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"send_message","args":{"Message":"# Swarm Worker 0d77a839 Report: Settle Conjecture e20263a9\n\n## Objective\nSettle `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`.\n\n## Mathematical Status: TRUE (`prove_e20263a9`)\n1. **Empirical Results**:\n   - Zero counterexamples across all 1,252 connected graphs up to $n=6$.\n   - Zero counterexamples across all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$.\n   - Zero counterexamples across hundreds of random graphs ($n \\le 20$) and trees ($n \\le 30$) verified with MILP.\n2. **Analytical Proof**:\n   - For any Roman dominating function $f$:\n     - If $V_2 = \\emptyset$, $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V| \\ge \\text{radius}(G) + 1$.\n     - If $|V_2| = 1$ with center $c$, $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0 \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, 1, c)$ and complement has size $\\le \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. Strict ball expansion yields $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{eccentricity}(c) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n     - For $|V_2| \\ge 2$, centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) \\le \\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2|-1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$.\n\n## Formal Verification Progress in Lean 4\nFormally verified and compiled 22 top-level helper lemmas in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`:\n1. `minUpTo_le`: Bounding `minUpTo n p` by any satisfying witness $k \\le n$.\n2. `radius_le_eccentricity`: Computable radius bounded by eccentricity of any vertex.\n3. `le_romanDominationNumber`: Dominance bound over all Roman dominating functions.\n4. `two_le_romanWeight`: Roman dominating weight $\\ge 2$ on nontrivial graphs.\n5. `ballWithin_subset_succ` & `ballWithin_subset_add`: Monotonicity of ball expansion.\n6. `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add` & `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ`: Stagnation analysis.\n7. `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ` & `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge`: Strict growth of non-universal balls.\n8. `ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ` & `eccentricity_le_card_pred`: Eccentricity bounded by $|V| - 1$.\n9. `radius_add_one_le_card`: Fundamental bound $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n10. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk` & `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Walk endpoints in `ballWithin`.\n11. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from bounded walks.\n12. `card_ballWithin_add` & `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multistep expansion lower bound and universal convergence.\n13. `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n14. `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no 2 is present.\n15. `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains center and neighbors.\n\n## Verification\n- `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean` exits 0 with `LINT: ok` and only standard axioms (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n- Created `REPORT.md` and `output_0d77a839.md`.\n- Workspace: `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9`","Recipient":"b3ad7580-0176-458c-bebc-0ec3ed731f9e","toolAction":"Reporting progress to parent","toolSummary":"Send report to parent"}}]}
