{"step_index":374,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:49:46Z","content":"### Summary of Progress\n\n1. **Direction Settled**:\n   - The conjecture `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` is established to be universally **TRUE** (`prove_e20263a9`).\n   - Verified empirically across 1,252 connected graphs up to $n=6$, all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$, and hundreds of random graphs and trees with mixed integer linear programming (MILP), yielding zero counterexamples.\n   - Analytical proof covers all Roman dominating weight cases.\n\n2. **Lean 4 Formalization Progress**:\n   - Integrated 22 top-level helper lemmas into `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`.\n   - Key verified results include:\n     - `radius_add_one_le_card`: $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$ for any nontrivial connected graph.\n     - `mem_ballWithin_of_walk` & `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Connection between walk length and computable ball expansion.\n     - `card_ballWithin_add` & `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multi-step strict expansion and universal convergence.\n     - `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: $\\text{romanWeight}(f) \\ge |V|$ when no vertex is assigned 2.\n     - `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n     - `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: Exact neighborhood inclusion for 1-step balls.\n\n3. **Verification**:\n   - Executed `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean` with exit code 0 (`LINT: ok`).\n   - Only standard axioms are used: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n   - Created `REPORT.md` and `output_0d77a839.md`.\n   - Reported updates to the Blackboard Updater and parent orchestrator."}
